/T (The emotion detection module \(detect.py\)loads the serialized model from emotion_model.h5 and initializes OpenCV'sHaar Cascade face detector. Each frame captured from the webcam is converted to grayscale for face detection. Detected face bounding boxes are used to crop the corresponding RGB region, which is then resized to 96x96, normalized, and expanded to a batch dimension before being passed to the model.  The model outputs a probability vector of length 7. The argmax of this vector  determines the predicted emotion class. The emotion label and bounding box )
/E (The emotion detection module \(detect.py\)loads the serialized model from emotion_model.h5 and initializes OpenCV'sHaar Cascade face detector. Each frame captured from the webcam is converted to grayscale for face detection. Detected face bounding boxes are used to crop the corresponding RGB region, which is then resized to 96x96, normalized, and expanded to a batch dimension before being passed to the model.  The model outputs a probability vector of length 7. The argmax of this vector  determines the predicted emotion class. The emotion label and bounding box )
