/T (  The results demonstrate that the system achieves strong performance on high- frequency emotion classes, with happy achieving an F1-score of 0.85 and  surprise achieving 0.79. Reasonable performance is obtained on challenging  classes such as fear at 0.47 and sad at 0.54. The relatively lower recall for fear  and sad classes is consistent with findings in the broader FER literature, as  these emotions share similar facial action units with neutral and angry  expressions respectivel )
